":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"FixedWidthInteger","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with k odd-degree vertices, every distance d between two of them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"satisfies k · (2 · d + 1) ≤ ","type":"text"},{"code":"W.max \/ 8","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the matching’s bound), checked as each distance is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"found.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","style":"note"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(k (n + m) log n) for the searches and O(k³) for the matching, with k the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number of odd-degree vertices; O(n + m + k²) memory."}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Complexity","style":"note"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"The shortest closed walk through every edge at least once (the Chinese postman problem),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by Edmonds and Johnson’s algorithm, or nil when the graph has no edge or its edges are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"all connected. Isolated vertices are ignored.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5ToursE18chinesePostmanTour6weightAD0eF0Vy6VertexQz5Edges_5IndexQZqd__GSgqd__AMXE_tSZRd__lF","title":"chinesePostmanTour(weight:)","roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"Tours","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"ChinesePostman.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tours\/ChinesePostman.swift#L239"},"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"chinesePostmanTour","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"extern